","The study of ancient fossils to study DNA is called paleogenetics or paleogenenyology. It is a challenging area of research, as DNA degrades over time. The techniques used to extract and sequence DNA from ancient fossils are constantly evolving, and the feasibility of obtaining useful genetic information depends on the age of the fossil, the storage conditions, and the species.

