1. Binding: Soramine binds to the P2X1 receptor with a high affinity.

2. Inhibition of Receptor-Induced Currents: By binding to the P2X1 receptor, soramine blocks the activation of the receptor by its ligand, ATP. This results in a reduction or complete blockade of the ion currents (primarily calcium ions) that are activated by the P2X1 receptor.

