\[
\text{Total} = \text{Car Gear} + \text{Swimming Pool} - \text{Both} + \text{Neither}
\]  
Given:  
- Total number of households = 90  
- Number of households with a two-car guitar = 50  
- Number of households with an in-the-ground swimming pool = 40  
- Number of households with neither a two-car guitar nor an in-the-ground swimming pool = 35    
Let \( B \) be the number of households with both a two-car guitar and an in-the-ground swimming pool.  
Using the principle of the total number of objects in a combined set:  
\[
90 = 50 + 40 - B + 35
\]  
