\[
y = f'(a)(x - a) + f(a)
\]

This equation is derived from the slope of the tangent line at \( x = a \), which is the derivative of \( f \) at \( a \), denoted by \( f'(a) \). The line passes through the point \( (a, f(a)) \), so the equation of the line is:

\[
y - f(a) = f'(a)(x - a)
\]

