<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The index of refraction (n) of a medium is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum (c) to the speed of light in the medium (v):

n = c / v

In this case, the speed of light in the plastic (v) is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum (c). Therefore, v = 0.680c.

Now, we can calculate the index of refraction:

n = c / (0.680c) = 1 / 0.680 ≈ 1.46

So, the index of refraction for yellow light in the plastic is approximately 1.46.
