   \[
   A = \pi \left(\frac{d}{2}\right)^2 = \pi \left(\frac{0.1 \text{ mm}}{2}\right)^2 = \pi (0.05 \text{ mm})^2 = 7.85 \times 10^{-6} \text{mm}^2
   \]
   Convert to cm²:
   \[
   A = 7.85 \times 10^{-6} \text{mm}^2 \times \left(\frac{1 \text{ cm}}{10 \text{ mm}}\right)^2 = 7.85 \times 10^{-8} \text{cm}^2
   \]

2. **Convert the flow rate to cm³/s:**
   \[
   10 \text{ cm³ min}^{-1} \times \left(\frac{1 \text{ min}}{60 \text{ s}}\right) = 1.67 \times 10^{-1} \text{ cm³ s}^{-1}
   \]

3. **Calculate the flow velocity:**
   \[
   v = \frac{\text{Flow Rate}}{\text{Area}} = \frac{0.167 \text{ cm³ s}^{-1}}{7.85 \times 10^{-8} \text{cm}^2} = 2.12 \times 10^5 \text{ cm s}^{-1}
   \]

4. **Calculate the reaction times for the given flow tube lengths:**
   - For 1 cm:
     \[
     \text{Reaction Time} = \frac{1 \text{ cm}}{2.12 \times 10^5 \text{ cm s}^{-1}} = 4.7 \times 10^{-6} \text{ s}
     \]
