   The energy released by the HMTM explosion is given by the formula:
   \[
   E = \frac{3}{2}PV
   \]
   where \( P = 1.0 \times 10^6 \text{ Pa} \), \( V = 1.0 \text{ L} = 1.0 \times 10^{-3} \text{ m}^3 \), and \( \gamma = 1.4 \).
   Substituting the values:
   \[
   E = \frac{3}{2} \times 1.0 \times 10^6 \times 1.0 \times 10^{-3} = 1500 \text{ J}
   \]

2. **Account for the 70% energy in the pressure wave**:
   Only 70% of the energy is in the pressure wave, so the energy released in the pressure wave is:
   \[
   E_{\text{wave}} = 0.7 \times 1500 = 1050 \text{ J}
   \]

3. **Determine the grams of TNT equivalent to the pressure wave energy**:
   TNT has an energy release of 4680 J/g. The grams of TNT equivalent to the pressure wave energy is:
   \[
   \text{TNT} = \frac{1050}{4680} = 0.225 \text{ g}
   \]

