The distance \(d\) is the difference in the distance of the rays from the central axis, which is:
\[
d = 10 \, \text{cm} - 0 = 10 \, \text{cm}
\]

Substituting the values into the formula:
\[
\delta y = \frac{25 \, \text{cm}}{8} \times 10 \, \text{cm} = 31.25 \, \text{cm}
