An engine working on the Otto cycle has an air standard cycle efficiency of 56% and rejects 544 kJ/kg of air. The pressure and temperature of air at the beginning of compression are 0.1 MPa and 60°C respectively. Compute:
1. The compression ratio of the engine.
2. The work done per kg of air.
3. The pressure and temperature at the end of compression.
4. The maximum pressure in the cycle.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","1. **Compression Ratio**:
   The efficiency of the Otto cycle is given by:
   \[
   \eta = 1 - \frac{1}{r^{\gamma - 1}}
   \]
   where \( \eta = 0.56 \), and \( r = \text{compression ratio} \), and \( \gamma = 1.4 \) (for air).
   Rearranging to solve for \( r \):
   \[
   r = \frac{1}{1 - \eta} = \frac{1}{1 - 0.56} = \frac{1}{0.44} = 2.27
   \]
   The compression ratio is \(\boxed{2.27}\).

2. **Work Done per kg of Air**:
   The heat rejected per kg of air is \( Q_{\text{reject}} = 544 \, \text{kJ/kg} \).
   The efficiency is also given by:
   \[
   \eta = \frac{W_{\text{net}}}{Q_{\text{input}}} = 1 - \frac{Q_{\text{reject}}}{Q_{\text{input}}}
   \]
   Solving for \( Q_{\text{input}} \):
   \[
   Q_{\text{input}} = \frac{Q_{\text{reject}}}{1 - \eta} = \frac{544}{1 - 0.56} = \frac{544}{0.44} = 1235.56 \, \text{kJ/kg}
   \]
   The net work is:
   \[
   W_{\text{net}} = \eta Q_{\text{input}} = 0.56 \times 1235.56 = 692 \, \text{kJ/kg}
   \]
   The work done per kg of air is \(\boxed{692 \, \text{kJ/kg}}\).

3. **Pressure and Temperature at the End of Compression**:
   Using the isentropic compression relation:
   \[
   \frac{T_2}{T_1} = \frac{P_2}{P_1}^{\gamma - 1}
   \]
   Given \( T_1 = 60^\circ \text{C} = 333 \, \text{K} \), \( P_1 = 0.1 \, \text{MPa} \), and \( r = 2.27 \), we find \( P_2 \) and \( T_2 \):
   \[
   P_2 = P_1 \times r = 0.1 \times 2.27 = 0.227 \, \text{MPa}
   \]
   \[
   T_2 = T_1 \times r^{\gamma - 1} = 333 \times (2.27)^{1.4 - 1} = 333 \times (2.27)^{0.4} = 333 \times 1.42 = 474.46 \, \text{K}
   \]
   The pressure at the end of compression is \(\boxed{0.227 \, \text{MPa}}\), and the temperature is \(\boxed{474.46 \, \text{K}}\).

4. **Maximum Pressure in the Cycle**:
   The maximum pressure occurs at the end of the compression process (compression stroke)",fluency,"# Task Description
