   \]

4. **Entropy (\(S\))**:
   The entropy of an ideal gas is given by:
   \[
   S = Nk \left[\ln\left(\frac{V}{N \lambda^3}\right) + \frac{5}{2}\right]
   \]
   Using \(V = \frac{NkT}{p}\):
   \[
   S = Nk \left[\ln\left(\frac{kT}{p \lambda^3}\right) + \frac{5}{2}\right]
   \]
   Substituting the values:
   \[
   S = 6.022 \times 10^{23} \times 1.381 \times 10^{-23} \left[\ln\left(\frac{1.381 \times 10^{-23} \times 290}{1 \times 10^5 \times (7.28 \times 10^{-11})^3}\right) + \frac{5}{2}\right] \approx 126 \text{ J/K}
   \]

