","The standard free energy change for the hydrolysis of ATP is calculated using the following equation:

ΔG = ΔG° (ATP + Pi → ADP + P)

where ΔG° (ATP + Pi → ADP + P) is the standard free energy change for the hydrolysis of ATP to ADP and pyrophosphate (P), which can be calculated from the standard free energy changes of the reactions of ATP → ADP + P and P + H2O → 2H+ + P2.

First, we need to calculate the standard free energy change for the hydrolysis of ATP to ADP and P:

ΔG°(ATP + Pi → ADP + P) = ΔG°(ADP + P → ATP) + ΔG°(H2O → 2H+ + P2)

We are given that ΔG°(ADP + Pi → ATP) = +30.5 kJ/mol (since the reaction is endergonic).

The standard free energy change for the hydrolysis of pyrophosphate (P2) to two phosphate ions (P) is:

ΔG°(P2 + H2O → 2P) = -10.5 kJ/mol

